"""The hooks' ``hub.json`` and ``hub.local.json`` reader: stdlib only, Python 3.9, never raises.

Hooks run on the system ``python3`` (3.9 on macOS) with no dependencies, so this module imports
nothing outside the standard library and nothing else from agent-hub; agent-hub's tests run it on
a real 3.9 and lint it with ruff at ``--target-version py39``. A hook must never fail because of
``hub.json`` (docs/design/project-config.md § Readers): where ``HubConfig`` would reject the file,
this reader falls back instead.

- A key that is absent, of the wrong type, or an empty string takes its default, and only that
  key: the rest of the file is kept. A list with any item that is not a string is ``()``.
- ``tracker.team_keys`` is ``tracker.teams`` when it is a non-empty list of non-empty strings,
  else ``(team,)`` when ``tracker.team`` is a non-empty string, else ``()``; ``team`` keeps its
  own value (``""`` when ``teams`` is set).
- The defaults of optional keys equal ``HubConfig``'s (the consistency test is
  ``packages/generator/tests/integration/test_hub_json_reader.py``). Required strings default
  to ``""``, ``project.name`` to the name of the directory holding the file (then ``hub``), and a
  repo without a non-empty string ``dir`` is dropped.
- ``platform.version`` counts only as three ASCII numbers (``0.2.0``); anything else is ``None``.
- ``platform.repository`` is the value as written when it is a string of at most 200 characters
  with the model's pattern; else ``None``. Present but not that (``null`` and ``""`` included),
  it also sets ``has_bad_repository``, which the hook reports instead of using the default.
- ``repos[].check_fast_timeout`` counts only as a JSON integer from 1 to 160; anything else is
  ``None``, the gate's default.
- ``repos[].check_stop`` is the string as written when it holds no control character and is
  UTF-8 text (``FREE_STRING``); anything else is ``""``, and the Stop gate runs ``check_fast``.
  A blank string is kept as it is: the gate strips it.
- A repo's ``default_branch`` is its effective value: its own when it is a string matching the
  model's branch pattern, else the ``project`` section's ``default_branch`` (it inherits).
- ``guard.readable_env_files`` keeps only the names that match the model's ``EnvFileName``
  (``.env.<suffix>``, not ending in a key-file suffix such as ``.pem``), so a bad ``hub.json`` never
  releases another file; ``secret_env_files``
  keeps its strings as written (they only tighten).
- ``guard.infra`` is ``None`` when absent. Present, ``InfraSection.problem`` names the first value
  the guard cannot use, and that key's tuple is ``()``: ``guard.infra`` when it is not an object
  (``null`` included), ``guard.infra.<key>`` when its value is not a list (``null`` included), and
  ``guard.infra.<key>[<i>]`` for an item that is not a string, is blank, holds a control
  character or is not valid UTF-8 (a lone surrogate). A key under it other than ``allow``,
  ``prod_markers`` and comment keys is unusable (``guard.infra.<key>``): a misspelled key must not
  drop a list silently. "First" is in document order. Patterns are compiled by the guard, not here.
- ``guard.blocked_words``, ``blocked_words_files`` and ``blocked_words_env`` keep a list only when
  every item has the model's shape and the list is within the model's length; else that list is
  ``()`` and ``GuardSection.problem`` names the first unusable location (``guard.<key>`` or
  ``guard.<key>[<i>]``), or a key under ``guard`` the model does not know (``guard.<key>``, the
  key shown only when it is lowercase letters, digits and ``_``, else the literal ``<key>``), in
  document order; a ``guard`` that is not an object is ``guard``. The guard asks while it is set (docs/design/environments.md § Fail closed).
- ``environments`` keeps each entry whose name is a safe segment of at most 40 characters, whose
  ``access`` is ``read``, ``write`` or ``ask`` and whose ``production`` (default ``false``) is a
  boolean; any other entry is dropped. ``credential_env`` keeps the ``credentials.env`` items with
  the model's variable-name shape.
- ``env_files`` and ``endpoints`` (also ``load_local_targets`` for ``hub.local.json``): each
  ``credentials.env_file`` of an environment, then of a ``repos[].services`` endpoint, once per path
  with the first environment naming it; and each endpoint's host (lowercase, from its ``url``) and
  ``resource``. An entry is kept only under a safe environment name; a path only with the model's
  ``EnvFilePath`` shape (no ``..`` segment, no leading ``/`` or ``~``, no secret shape), a url only
  with the model's ``Url`` shape, a resource only as non-blank text without a control character or
  secret shape; anything else is dropped, and only that entry. Whether the environment is declared
  is not checked: the guard only tightens with them (docs/design/scenarios.md § Credentials).
- Elsewhere, unknown keys and comment keys (``_`` first) are ignored. ``modules`` and
  ``doctor.rules`` keep each entry's settings, minus comment keys, without checking them.
- ``hub.local.json`` (one developer's ``project.branch_prefix``, ``author_name``,
  ``author_email`` and ``tracker.transport``) counts only as a regular file of at most
  ``LOCAL_FILE_MAX_BYTES``; otherwise it sets nothing. A local value counts only when it is a
  string with the model's shape (pattern, or ``api``/``mcp``), else that key falls through.
  ``EffectiveValues`` gives each key from ``hub.local.json``, else ``hub.json``, else git config
  (asked lazily, once per key); with no prefix in a file, the prefix is the effective email's
  local part plus ``/`` when that is a valid prefix (docs/design/developer-identity.md).

- ``load_local_layer`` reads ``hub.local.json``'s ``environments`` (as above, but an entry
  without ``access`` is kept with ``""``: it may tighten a committed one) and its three blocked
  lists (as above; any other key under ``guard`` is unusable, since only those are local). A file
  that exists but is not a regular file of at most ``LOCAL_FILE_MAX_BYTES`` holding a JSON object
  sets ``file_problem``; an absent one sets nothing.

- ``read_lock_source`` gives the source ``<repository>@<commit>#subdirectory=packages/agent-hub``
  of the release commit ``hub.lock`` records (ADR 0054), only when the lock is a regular file
  (not a link) of at most ``LOCK_FILE_MAX_BYTES`` holding a JSON object whose
  ``platform_commit`` is 40 lowercase hex, whose ``platform_version`` is ``platform.version`` and
  whose ``platform_repository`` is the repository in use (``platform.repository``, else the
  caller's ``default_repository``, the platform's own); else ``None``, and the caller uses the tag.

- ``read_brief_cache`` and ``read_refresh_cause`` read ``.hub-cache/brief.json`` (what
  ``hub brief --write-cache`` writes) and ``.hub-cache/refresh.json`` (what a failed SessionStart
  refresh writes; ADR 0055) as untrusted: only a regular file (not a link, in a folder that is not
  a link) of at most ``CACHE_FILE_MAX_BYTES`` holding a JSON object whose ``made_at`` is a finite
  number at most ``CACHE_FUTURE_SECONDS`` ahead of ``now``, and whose ``brief`` (cut at
  ``CACHE_BRIEF_MAX_CHARS``, then stripped, not empty) or ``cause`` (cut at
  ``REFRESH_CAUSE_MAX_CHARS``, then stripped, not empty) is a string; else ``None``.

A hook that loads this file by path must register the module before running it, or the frozen
dataclasses fail to build (``AttributeError`` on ``NoneType.__dict__``)::

    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("hub_stdlib_reader", path)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    sys.modules[spec.name] = module
    spec.loader.exec_module(module)
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import json
import math
import os
import re
import stat
from collections.abc import Callable
from dataclasses import dataclass, field

COMMENT_KEY_PREFIX = "_"
FALLBACK_PROJECT_NAME = "hub"
LOCAL_FILE = "hub.local.json"
LOCAL_FILE_MAX_BYTES = 65_536
TRANSPORTS = ("api", "mcp")
PREFIX_FROM_LOCAL = LOCAL_FILE
PREFIX_FROM_HUB = "hub.json"
PREFIX_DERIVED = "derived"
# ``[0-9]`` and ``fullmatch``: ``\d`` takes any Unicode digit and ``$`` a final newline.
RELEASE_VERSION = re.compile(r"[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+")
# The model's ``PlatformRepository`` pattern, for ``fullmatch``, rendered from agent-hub's core.
PLATFORM_REPOSITORY = re.compile(r"@@{platform_repository_pattern}")
PLATFORM_REPOSITORY_MAX_CHARS = 200
LOCK_FILE = "hub.lock"
LOCK_FILE_MAX_BYTES = 1_048_576
RELEASE_COMMIT = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{40}")
RELEASE_SUBDIRECTORY = "#subdirectory=packages/agent-hub"
# The brief cache (ADR 0055): core's ``agent_hub.core.workspace.brief_cache`` writes the same names.
CACHE_FOLDER = ".hub-cache"
BRIEF_CACHE_FILE = "brief.json"
REFRESH_RECORD_FILE = "refresh.json"
CACHE_FILE_MAX_BYTES = 65_536
CACHE_BRIEF_MAX_CHARS = 8000
REFRESH_CAUSE_MAX_CHARS = 200
# A clock a little behind the writer's still reads its file; one far ahead of it does not.
CACHE_FUTURE_SECONDS = 60
# The model's bounds for ``repos[].check_fast_timeout``.
CHECK_FAST_TIMEOUT_MIN = 1
CHECK_FAST_TIMEOUT_MAX = 160
# The model's ``BranchName`` pattern without ``^`` and ``$``, for ``fullmatch``. No separator
# character is also a segment character, so ``re`` matches in linear time.
BRANCH_NAME = re.compile(
    r"[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:[.-][A-Za-z0-9_]+)*(?:/[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:[.-][A-Za-z0-9_]+)*)*"
)
# The model's ``BranchPrefix``, ``EmailAddress`` and ``FreeString`` patterns, likewise.
BRANCH_PREFIX = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:[.-][A-Za-z0-9_]+)*/")
EMAIL_ADDRESS = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+")
FREE_STRING = re.compile(r"[^\x00-\x1f\x7f]+")
# The model's ``EnvFileName`` pattern without ``^`` and ``$``: an env file name with a suffix.
ENV_FILE_NAME = re.compile(r"\.env\.[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+")
# The model's ``KEY_FILE_SUFFIXES``: a readable env file name never ends in one.
KEY_FILE_SUFFIXES = (".pem", ".key", ".p12", ".pfx")
# A character ``FREE_STRING`` refuses: an infra pattern holding one is unusable.
CONTROL_CHARACTER = re.compile(r"[\x00-\x1f\x7f]")
# The keys ``guard.infra`` may hold besides comment keys; any other key is unusable.
INFRA_LISTS = ("allow", "prod_markers")
# The git config key each git-read identity key comes from.
GIT_KEYS = {"author_name": "user.name", "author_email": "user.email"}
# The model's ``Guard`` keys (core/hub_config/model.py), in its order: any other key under
# ``guard`` is unusable for the blocked lists.
GUARD_KEYS = (
    "ask_before_edit",
    "deny_hosts",
    "deny_paths",
    "readable_env_files",
    "secret_env_files",
    "infra",
    "blocked_words",
    "blocked_words_files",
    "blocked_words_env",
)
BLOCKED_LISTS = ("blocked_words", "blocked_words_files", "blocked_words_env")
# An unknown ``guard`` key is named in a problem only with this shape; any other is ``<key>``, so
# a secret pasted as a key never reaches a reason.
PLAIN_GUARD_KEY = re.compile(r"[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,40}")
# The model's ``BlockedWord``, ``WordFileGlob`` and ``EnvVarPattern`` shapes and bounds
# (core/hub_config/environments.py), for ``fullmatch``. No separator character is also a segment
# character, so ``re`` matches in linear time.
BLOCKED_WORD = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9]+(?:[-_.][A-Za-z0-9]+)*")
BLOCKED_WORD_MIN_CHARS = 2
BLOCKED_WORD_MAX_CHARS = 64
MAX_BLOCKED_WORDS = 200
BLOCKED_GLOB = re.compile(r"[!-.0-~][!-~]*")
BLOCKED_GLOB_MAX_CHARS = 200
MAX_BLOCKED_GLOBS = 100
BLOCKED_ENV = re.compile(r"[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}\*?")
MAX_BLOCKED_ENV = 50
# The model's ``EnvironmentName`` (a safe segment of at most 40 characters), ``Access`` and
# ``EnvVarName`` (core/hub_config/environments.py), for ``fullmatch``.
ENVIRONMENT_NAME = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9_]+(?:[.-][A-Za-z0-9_]+)*")
ENVIRONMENT_NAME_MAX_CHARS = 40
ACCESS_LEVELS = ("read", "write", "ask")
ENV_VAR_NAME = re.compile(r"[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}")
# The model's ``EnvFilePath`` (printable ASCII without space, not starting with ``/`` or ``~``, at
# most 200 characters, no ``..`` segment) and ``Url`` (``scheme://host[:port][/path]``, no user
# info, query or fragment, at most 200 characters) shapes, for ``fullmatch``; the url's host is
# group 1.
ENV_FILE_PATH = re.compile(r"[!-.0-}][!-~]*")
ENV_FILE_PATH_MAX_CHARS = 200
ENDPOINT_URL = re.compile(
    r"[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*://([A-Za-z0-9.-]+)(?::[0-9]{1,5})?(?:/[!\"$->A-~]*)?"
)
ENDPOINT_URL_MAX_CHARS = 200
# core/secret_shapes.py's shapes that fit an environment name or a blocked word (letters, digits
# and -_. only): the private-key, credential-assignment and Fernet shapes need a space or "=".
# The JWT shape is the old lint's, which matches what core's linear rewrite matches; the texts
# it runs on are at most 64 characters.
SECRET_SHAPES = tuple(
    re.compile(pattern)
    for pattern in (
        r"eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{15,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{15}",
        r"AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}",
        r"\b(?:sk|pk)_(?:live|test)_[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}",
        r"\bsk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}",
        r"\bghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}",
        r"\blin_api_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}",
    )
)


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class PlatformSection:
    """``platform``: the release the hub is pinned to, ``None`` when absent or malformed.

    ``repository`` is the source as written, ``None`` when absent or bad; ``has_bad_repository``
    tells a bad one from an absent one.
    """

    version: str | None = None
    repository: str | None = None
    has_bad_repository: bool = False


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class ProjectSection:
    """``project``."""

    name: str = FALLBACK_PROJECT_NAME
    hub_repo: str = ""
    branch_prefix: str = ""
    default_branch: str = "main"
    author_name: str = ""
    author_email: str = ""


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class TrackerSection:
    """``tracker``: ``team_keys`` are the configured team keys in order, the first the default."""

    kind: str = ""
    team: str = ""
    team_keys: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    ready_label: str = "agent-ready"
    failed_label: str = "agent-failed"
    transport: str = "api"


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class RepoEntry:
    """One ``repos[]`` item; items without a ``dir`` are dropped.

    ``default_branch`` is the effective value: the repo's own, else the project's.
    """

    dir: str
    github: str = ""
    role: str = "app"
    check_fast: str = ""
    check_fast_timeout: int | None = None
    check_stop: str = ""
    check: str = ""
    default_branch: str = "main"


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class InfraSection:
    """``guard.infra``; ``problem`` names the first value the guard cannot use."""

    allow: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    prod_markers: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    problem: str = ""


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class GuardSection:
    """``guard``; ``infra`` is ``None`` when ``guard.infra`` is absent. ``problem`` names the first
    blocked list (or ``guard`` key) the guard cannot use, ``""`` when none."""

    ask_before_edit: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    deny_hosts: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    deny_paths: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    readable_env_files: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    secret_env_files: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    infra: InfraSection | None = None
    blocked_words: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    blocked_words_files: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    blocked_words_env: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    problem: str = ""


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class EnvironmentEntry:
    """One ``environments`` entry: its name, ``access`` (``""`` for a local entry without one),
    whether it is production, and the variable names of its ``credentials.env``."""

    name: str
    access: str
    production: bool = False
    credential_env: tuple[str, ...] = ()


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class EnvFileEntry:
    """A declared env file: its path relative to the workspace and the first environment naming it."""

    path: str
    environment: str


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class EndpointEntry:
    """A service's endpoint in one environment: its url's host (lowercase) and its resource, each
    ``""`` when absent."""

    environment: str
    host: str = ""
    resource: str = ""


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class EnvironmentTargets:
    """What a file's environments reach: their env files and their services' endpoints."""

    env_files: tuple[EnvFileEntry, ...] = ()
    endpoints: tuple[EndpointEntry, ...] = ()


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class DoctorSection:
    """``doctor``: each rule id with its settings, unchecked."""

    rules: dict[str, dict[str, object]] = field(default_factory=dict)


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class HubFile:
    """``hub.json`` as read by hooks; field names are the JSON keys."""

    schema_version: int | None = None
    platform: PlatformSection = field(default_factory=PlatformSection)
    project: ProjectSection = field(default_factory=ProjectSection)
    tracker: TrackerSection = field(default_factory=TrackerSection)
    repos: tuple[RepoEntry, ...] = ()
    guard: GuardSection = field(default_factory=GuardSection)
    environments: tuple[EnvironmentEntry, ...] = ()
    modules: dict[str, dict[str, object]] = field(default_factory=dict)
    doctor: DoctorSection = field(default_factory=DoctorSection)
    env_files: tuple[EnvFileEntry, ...] = ()
    endpoints: tuple[EndpointEntry, ...] = ()


def load_hub_file(path: str | os.PathLike[str]) -> HubFile:
    """Read ``hub.json`` at ``path``; never raises (see the module docstring for the defaults)."""
    document = _read_document(path)
    project = _object(document.get("project"))
    tracker = _object(document.get("tracker"))
    guard = _object(document.get("guard"))
    schema_version = document.get("schema_version")
    project_branch = _text(project, "default_branch", ProjectSection.default_branch)
    blocked, blocked_problem = _blocked(guard, GUARD_KEYS)
    blocked_problem = _guard_shape_problem(document) or blocked_problem
    targets = _targets(document)
    return HubFile(
        # ``bool`` is an ``int``; only a JSON integer is a schema version.
        schema_version=schema_version if type(schema_version) is int else None,
        platform=_platform(_object(document.get("platform"))),
        project=ProjectSection(
            name=_text(project, "name", _directory_name(path)),
            hub_repo=_text(project, "hub_repo", ""),
            branch_prefix=_text(project, "branch_prefix", ""),
            default_branch=project_branch,
            author_name=_text(project, "author_name", ""),
            author_email=_text(project, "author_email", ""),
        ),
        tracker=TrackerSection(
            kind=_text(tracker, "kind", ""),
            team=_text(tracker, "team", ""),
            team_keys=_team_keys(tracker),
            ready_label=_text(tracker, "ready_label", TrackerSection.ready_label),
            failed_label=_text(tracker, "failed_label", TrackerSection.failed_label),
            transport=_text(tracker, "transport", TrackerSection.transport),
        ),
        repos=_repos(document.get("repos"), project_branch),
        guard=GuardSection(
            ask_before_edit=_texts(guard, "ask_before_edit"),
            deny_hosts=_texts(guard, "deny_hosts"),
            deny_paths=_texts(guard, "deny_paths"),
            readable_env_files=tuple(
                name
                for name in _texts(guard, "readable_env_files")
                if ENV_FILE_NAME.fullmatch(name) and not name.endswith(KEY_FILE_SUFFIXES)
            ),
            secret_env_files=_texts(guard, "secret_env_files"),
            infra=_infra(guard),
            blocked_words=blocked.get("blocked_words", ()),
            blocked_words_files=blocked.get("blocked_words_files", ()),
            blocked_words_env=blocked.get("blocked_words_env", ()),
            problem=blocked_problem,
        ),
        environments=_environments(document.get("environments")),
        modules=_settings_by_id(document.get("modules")),
        doctor=DoctorSection(rules=_settings_by_id(_object(document.get("doctor")).get("rules"))),
        env_files=targets.env_files,
        endpoints=targets.endpoints,
    )


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class LocalFile:
    """``hub.local.json`` as read by hooks: each key's checked value, ``""`` when it sets none."""

    branch_prefix: str = ""
    author_name: str = ""
    author_email: str = ""
    transport: str = ""


def load_local_file(path: str | os.PathLike[str]) -> LocalFile:
    """Read ``hub.local.json`` at ``path``; never raises (see the module docstring)."""
    document = _read_document(path, max_bytes=LOCAL_FILE_MAX_BYTES)
    project = _object(document.get("project"))
    transport = _text(_object(document.get("tracker")), "transport", "")
    return LocalFile(
        branch_prefix=_matching(project, "branch_prefix", BRANCH_PREFIX),
        author_name=_matching(project, "author_name", FREE_STRING),
        author_email=_matching(project, "author_email", EMAIL_ADDRESS),
        transport=transport if transport in TRANSPORTS else "",
    )


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class LocalLayer:
    """``hub.local.json``'s environments and blocked lists, as the hooks add them to hub.json's.

    ``problem`` names the first blocked list (or ``guard`` key) the guard cannot use;
    ``file_problem`` is ``hub.local.json`` when the file exists but cannot be used as a whole,
    ``""`` when it is absent or usable.
    """

    environments: tuple[EnvironmentEntry, ...] = ()
    blocked_words: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    blocked_words_files: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    blocked_words_env: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    problem: str = ""
    file_problem: str = ""


def load_local_layer(path: str | os.PathLike[str]) -> LocalLayer:
    """Read ``hub.local.json``'s layer at ``path``; never raises (see the module docstring)."""
    if not os.path.lexists(path):
        return LocalLayer()
    document = _read_object(path, max_bytes=LOCAL_FILE_MAX_BYTES)
    if document is None:
        return LocalLayer(file_problem=LOCAL_FILE)
    lists, problem = _blocked(_object(document.get("guard")), BLOCKED_LISTS)
    problem = _guard_shape_problem(document) or problem
    return LocalLayer(
        environments=_environments(document.get("environments"), needs_access=False),
        blocked_words=lists.get("blocked_words", ()),
        blocked_words_files=lists.get("blocked_words_files", ()),
        blocked_words_env=lists.get("blocked_words_env", ()),
        problem=problem,
    )


def load_local_targets(path: str | os.PathLike[str]) -> EnvironmentTargets:
    """``hub.local.json``'s env files and endpoints at ``path``; none when the file is absent or
    cannot be used (the guard then asks for the file itself, ``LocalLayer.file_problem``)."""
    if not os.path.lexists(path):
        return EnvironmentTargets()
    document = _read_object(path, max_bytes=LOCAL_FILE_MAX_BYTES)
    return EnvironmentTargets() if document is None else _targets(document)


class EffectiveValues:
    """One developer's identity and transport: ``hub.local.json``, else ``hub.json``, else git.

    ``git_value(key)`` gives git's output for ``git config --get <key>`` (``user.name``,
    ``user.email``), ``""`` when unset or when git fails. It is called only for a key no file
    sets, at most once per key, and never while the object is built. Its value loses one
    trailing newline and then counts only with the model's shape. ``hub.json``'s values are used
    unchecked, as elsewhere in this reader; a derived prefix counts only when it matches
    ``BRANCH_PREFIX``. Every method gives ``""`` when no source gives a value.
    """

    def __init__(self, hub_file: HubFile, local_file: LocalFile, git_value: Callable[[str], str]):
        self.hub_file = hub_file
        self.local_file = local_file
        self.transport = local_file.transport or hub_file.tracker.transport
        self._git_value = git_value
        self._git: dict[str, str] = {}

    def author_name(self) -> str:
        return self._value("author_name", FREE_STRING)

    def author_email(self) -> str:
        return self._value("author_email", EMAIL_ADDRESS)

    def branch_prefix(self) -> str:
        """The file's prefix, else the effective email's local part plus ``/`` when valid."""
        from_file = self.local_file.branch_prefix or self.hub_file.project.branch_prefix
        if from_file:
            return from_file
        derived = self.author_email().rpartition("@")[0] + "/"
        return derived if BRANCH_PREFIX.fullmatch(derived) else ""

    def prefix_source(self) -> str:
        """``hub.local.json``, ``hub.json``, ``derived``, or ``""`` when there is no prefix."""
        if self.local_file.branch_prefix:
            return PREFIX_FROM_LOCAL
        if self.hub_file.project.branch_prefix:
            return PREFIX_FROM_HUB
        return PREFIX_DERIVED if self.branch_prefix() else ""

    def _value(self, key: str, pattern: re.Pattern[str]) -> str:
        from_file = getattr(self.local_file, key) or getattr(self.hub_file.project, key)
        if from_file:
            return from_file
        git_key = GIT_KEYS[key]
        if git_key not in self._git:
            value = self._git_value(git_key)
            # As the CLI: one trailing newline is git's own, anything else is the value's.
            value = value[:-1] if value.endswith("\n") else value
            self._git[git_key] = value if _is_shaped(value, pattern) else ""
        return self._git[git_key]


def _read_document(
    path: str | os.PathLike[str], max_bytes: int | None = None
) -> dict[str, object]:
    """The file's top-level object; ``{}`` when it cannot be read, is larger than ``max_bytes``
    or is not a JSON object."""
    document = _read_object(path, max_bytes)
    return {} if document is None else document


def _read_object(
    path: str | os.PathLike[str], max_bytes: int | None = None, *, follow_links: bool = True
) -> dict[str, object] | None:
    """The file's top-level object; ``None`` when it cannot be read, is larger than ``max_bytes``,
    is not a JSON object, or (``follow_links`` false) is a link."""
    # Only a regular file (a symlink to one included, unless ``follow_links`` is false): opening a
    # FIFO blocks and a device such as /dev/zero never ends, so a hook would hang. The check by
    # path skips the open; what was opened (without blocking) is checked again, so a FIFO swapped
    # in after it is not read.
    flags = os.O_RDONLY | getattr(os, "O_NONBLOCK", 0)
    if not follow_links:
        if os.path.islink(path):
            return None
        flags |= getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0)
    if not os.path.isfile(path):
        return None
    try:
        descriptor = os.open(path, flags)
        with open(descriptor, "rb") as file:
            if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(file.fileno()).st_mode):
                return None
            if max_bytes is None:
                content = file.read()
            else:
                # One byte more than allowed tells a file that grew after any size check.
                content = file.read(max_bytes + 1)
                if len(content) > max_bytes:
                    return None
        document = json.loads(content.decode("utf-8"))
    # OSError: missing, a directory, unreadable. ValueError: bad UTF-8 or JSON (and a NUL in the
    # path). RecursionError: nesting deeper than the parser's stack.
    except (OSError, ValueError, RecursionError):
        return None
    return _object(document) if isinstance(document, dict) else None


def _directory_name(path: str | os.PathLike[str]) -> str:
    """The name of the hub directory, the one holding the file (``hubhooks.py`` does the same)."""
    try:
        directory = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path))
    # A relative path needs the working directory, which may have been deleted.
    except OSError:
        return FALLBACK_PROJECT_NAME
    return os.path.basename(directory) or FALLBACK_PROJECT_NAME


def _object(value: object) -> dict[str, object]:
    """A JSON object without its comment keys; anything else is an empty object."""
    if not isinstance(value, dict):
        return {}
    return {key: item for key, item in value.items() if not key.startswith(COMMENT_KEY_PREFIX)}


def _text(section: dict[str, object], key: str, default: str) -> str:
    value = section.get(key)
    return value if isinstance(value, str) and value else default


def _matching(section: dict[str, object], key: str, pattern: re.Pattern[str]) -> str:
    """The value at ``key`` when it is a string with ``pattern``'s shape, else ``""``."""
    value = _text(section, key, "")
    return value if _is_shaped(value, pattern) else ""


def _is_shaped(value: str, pattern: re.Pattern[str]) -> bool:
    """Whether ``pattern`` matches all of ``value`` and ``value`` is UTF-8 text, as the model asks.

    A lone surrogate (JSON ``"\\ud800"``) passes a negated character class but not the model.
    """
    if not pattern.fullmatch(value):
        return False
    try:
        value.encode("utf-8", "strict")
    except UnicodeEncodeError:
        return False
    return True


def _bounded_int(section: dict[str, object], key: str, low: int, high: int) -> int | None:
    """The value at ``key`` when it is a JSON integer from ``low`` to ``high``, else ``None``."""
    value = section.get(key)
    if type(value) is int and low <= value <= high:
        return value
    return None


def _texts(section: dict[str, object], key: str) -> tuple[str, ...]:
    value = section.get(key)
    if isinstance(value, list) and all(isinstance(item, str) for item in value):
        return tuple(value)
    return ()


def _infra(guard: dict[str, object]) -> InfraSection | None:
    """``guard.infra``: ``None`` when absent; else its lists, with the first unusable location."""
    if "infra" not in guard:
        return None
    infra = guard["infra"]
    if not isinstance(infra, dict):
        return InfraSection(problem="guard.infra")
    lists: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {}
    first_problem = ""
    # Keys in document order: the problem is the first unusable one. An unknown key (a misspelled
    # ``prod_markers`` would drop the markers: fail open) is unusable as a whole.
    for key, value in _object(infra).items():
        if key in INFRA_LISTS:
            lists[key], problem = _patterns(key, value)
        else:
            problem = "guard.infra." + key
        first_problem = first_problem or problem
    return InfraSection(
        allow=lists.get("allow", ()),
        prod_markers=lists.get("prod_markers", ()),
        problem=first_problem,
    )


def _patterns(key: str, value: object) -> tuple[tuple[str, ...], str]:
    """``value`` as a tuple and ``""``; ``()`` and the location of the first unusable value."""
    location = "guard.infra." + key
    if not isinstance(value, list):
        return (), location
    for index, item in enumerate(value):
        if not _usable_pattern(item):
            return (), f"{location}[{index}]"
    return tuple(value), ""


def _usable_pattern(item: object) -> bool:
    """A non-blank string with no control character that encodes as UTF-8 (no lone surrogate)."""
    if not isinstance(item, str) or not item.strip() or CONTROL_CHARACTER.search(item):
        return False
    try:
        item.encode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeEncodeError:
        return False
    return True


def _blocked(
    guard: dict[str, object], known: tuple[str, ...]
) -> tuple[dict[str, tuple[str, ...]], str]:
    """The blocked lists under ``guard`` and the first unusable location, in document order: a
    list that is not a list or is too long, a bad item, or a key not in ``known`` (a misspelled
    list must not drop its words silently). An unusable list is ``()``."""
    lists: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {}
    first_problem = ""
    for key, value in guard.items():
        if key in BLOCKED_LISTS:
            lists[key], problem = _blocked_list(key, value)
        else:
            shown = key if PLAIN_GUARD_KEY.fullmatch(key) else "<key>"
            problem = "" if key in known else "guard." + shown
        first_problem = first_problem or problem
    return lists, first_problem


def _guard_shape_problem(document: dict[str, object]) -> str:
    """``guard`` when the file has a ``guard`` that is not an object (its words would vanish)."""
    if "guard" in document and not isinstance(document["guard"], dict):
        return "guard"
    return ""


def _blocked_list(key: str, value: object) -> tuple[tuple[str, ...], str]:
    """``value`` as a tuple and ``""``; ``()`` and the location of the first unusable value."""
    location = "guard." + key
    usable, limit = BLOCKED_SHAPES[key]
    if not isinstance(value, list) or len(value) > limit:
        return (), location
    for index, item in enumerate(value):
        if not isinstance(item, str) or not usable(item):
            return (), f"{location}[{index}]"
    return tuple(value), ""


def secret_shaped(text: str) -> bool:
    """Whether ``text`` (a name or a word) holds a secret's shape, as core's ``secret_kind``."""
    return any(shape.search(text) for shape in SECRET_SHAPES)


def _is_blocked_word(item: str) -> bool:
    # A secret-shaped word is unusable, so the guard asks, as the CLI refuses it.
    return (
        BLOCKED_WORD_MIN_CHARS <= len(item) <= BLOCKED_WORD_MAX_CHARS
        and bool(BLOCKED_WORD.fullmatch(item))
        and not secret_shaped(item)
    )


def _is_blocked_glob(item: str) -> bool:
    return (
        len(item) <= BLOCKED_GLOB_MAX_CHARS
        and bool(BLOCKED_GLOB.fullmatch(item))
        and ".." not in item.split("/")
    )


def _is_blocked_env(item: str) -> bool:
    return bool(BLOCKED_ENV.fullmatch(item))


# Each blocked list's item check and its most items.
BLOCKED_SHAPES: dict[str, tuple[Callable[[str], bool], int]] = {
    "blocked_words": (_is_blocked_word, MAX_BLOCKED_WORDS),
    "blocked_words_files": (_is_blocked_glob, MAX_BLOCKED_GLOBS),
    "blocked_words_env": (_is_blocked_env, MAX_BLOCKED_ENV),
}


def _environments(value: object, *, needs_access: bool = True) -> tuple[EnvironmentEntry, ...]:
    """Each entry with a usable name, ``access`` and ``production``; the others are dropped. With
    ``needs_access`` false (``hub.local.json``), an entry without ``access`` is kept with ``""``."""
    entries = []
    for name, item in _object(value).items():
        if len(name) > ENVIRONMENT_NAME_MAX_CHARS or not ENVIRONMENT_NAME.fullmatch(name):
            continue
        if not isinstance(item, dict):
            continue
        environment = _object(item)
        access = environment.get("access", None if needs_access else "")
        production = environment.get("production", False)
        usable = ACCESS_LEVELS if needs_access else ACCESS_LEVELS + ("",)
        if not isinstance(access, str) or access not in usable or not isinstance(production, bool):
            continue
        names = _object(environment.get("credentials")).get("env")
        credential_env = tuple(
            text
            for text in (names if isinstance(names, list) else [])
            if isinstance(text, str) and ENV_VAR_NAME.fullmatch(text)
        )
        entries.append(EnvironmentEntry(name, access, production, credential_env))
    return tuple(entries)


def _environment_name(name: object) -> bool:
    return (
        isinstance(name, str)
        and len(name) <= ENVIRONMENT_NAME_MAX_CHARS
        and _is_shaped(name, ENVIRONMENT_NAME)
        and not secret_shaped(name)
    )


def _env_file(credentials: object) -> str:
    """``credentials.env_file`` when it has the model's ``EnvFilePath`` shape, else ``""``."""
    value = _object(credentials).get("env_file")
    if (
        not isinstance(value, str)
        or len(value) > ENV_FILE_PATH_MAX_CHARS
        or not _is_shaped(value, ENV_FILE_PATH)
        or ".." in value.split("/")
        or secret_shaped(value)
    ):
        return ""
    return value


def _endpoint(environment: str, item: object) -> EndpointEntry | None:
    """The endpoint's host and resource; ``None`` when neither is usable."""
    endpoint = _object(item)
    url, resource = endpoint.get("url"), endpoint.get("resource")
    host = ""
    if isinstance(url, str) and len(url) <= ENDPOINT_URL_MAX_CHARS and not secret_shaped(url):
        found = ENDPOINT_URL.fullmatch(url)
        host = found.group(1).lower() if found and _is_shaped(url, ENDPOINT_URL) else ""
    if not (isinstance(resource, str) and resource.strip() and _is_shaped(resource, FREE_STRING)) or (
        secret_shaped(resource)
    ):
        resource = ""
    return EndpointEntry(environment, host, resource) if host or resource else None


def _targets(document: dict[str, object]) -> EnvironmentTargets:
    """The env files (environments' first, then endpoints', each path once) and the endpoints of
    ``environments`` and ``repos[].services``; a bad entry is dropped, and only that entry."""
    env_files: dict[str, str] = {}
    endpoints = []
    for name, item in _object(document.get("environments")).items():
        path = _env_file(_object(item).get("credentials"))
        if _environment_name(name) and path:
            env_files.setdefault(path, name)
    repos = document.get("repos")
    for repo in repos if isinstance(repos, list) else []:
        for service in _object(_object(repo).get("services")).values():
            for name, item in _object(_object(service).get("endpoints")).items():
                if not _environment_name(name):
                    continue
                path = _env_file(_object(item).get("credentials"))
                if path:
                    env_files.setdefault(path, name)
                endpoint = _endpoint(name, item)
                if endpoint is not None:
                    endpoints.append(endpoint)
    return EnvironmentTargets(
        env_files=tuple(EnvFileEntry(path, name) for path, name in env_files.items()),
        endpoints=tuple(endpoints),
    )


def _team_keys(tracker: dict[str, object]) -> tuple[str, ...]:
    """``teams`` when every item is a non-empty string, else ``(team,)``, else ``()``."""
    teams = _texts(tracker, "teams")
    if teams and all(teams):
        return teams
    team = _text(tracker, "team", "")
    return (team,) if team else ()


def _platform(platform: dict[str, object]) -> PlatformSection:
    version = _version(platform)
    if "repository" not in platform:
        return PlatformSection(version=version)
    value = platform["repository"]
    if (
        isinstance(value, str)
        and len(value) <= PLATFORM_REPOSITORY_MAX_CHARS
        and _is_shaped(value, PLATFORM_REPOSITORY)
    ):
        return PlatformSection(version=version, repository=value)
    return PlatformSection(version=version, has_bad_repository=True)


def read_lock_source(
    hub: str | os.PathLike[str], platform: PlatformSection, default_repository: str
) -> str | None:
    """The source of the release commit ``hub.lock`` records for ``platform``, else ``None``
    (see the module docstring); never raises."""
    if platform.version is None or platform.has_bad_repository:
        return None
    repository = platform.repository or default_repository
    lock = _read_object(
        os.path.join(hub, LOCK_FILE), max_bytes=LOCK_FILE_MAX_BYTES, follow_links=False
    )
    if lock is None:
        return None
    commit = lock.get("platform_commit")
    if not (isinstance(commit, str) and RELEASE_COMMIT.fullmatch(commit)):
        return None
    if lock.get("platform_version") != platform.version:
        return None
    if lock.get("platform_repository") != repository:
        return None
    return repository + "@" + commit + RELEASE_SUBDIRECTORY


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class BriefCache:
    """The brief cache: when it was made (seconds since the epoch) and its brief."""

    made_at: float
    brief: str


def read_brief_cache(hub: str | os.PathLike[str], now: float) -> BriefCache | None:
    """The hub's brief cache, else ``None`` (see the module docstring); never raises."""
    found = _cache_document(hub, BRIEF_CACHE_FILE, "brief", CACHE_BRIEF_MAX_CHARS, now)
    return None if found is None else BriefCache(made_at=found[0], brief=found[1])


def read_refresh_cause(hub: str | os.PathLike[str], now: float) -> str | None:
    """The cause the last failed refresh recorded, else ``None``; never raises."""
    found = _cache_document(hub, REFRESH_RECORD_FILE, "cause", REFRESH_CAUSE_MAX_CHARS, now)
    return None if found is None else found[1]


def _cache_document(
    hub: str | os.PathLike[str], name: str, key: str, max_chars: int, now: float
) -> tuple[float, str] | None:
    """(``made_at``, the text under ``key`` cut at ``max_chars``) of a ``.hub-cache`` file."""
    folder = os.path.join(hub, CACHE_FOLDER)
    if os.path.islink(folder):  # the CLI refuses a linked folder; so does the reader
        return None
    document = _read_object(
        os.path.join(folder, name), max_bytes=CACHE_FILE_MAX_BYTES, follow_links=False
    )
    if document is None:
        return None
    made_at = document.get("made_at")
    if isinstance(made_at, bool) or not isinstance(made_at, (int, float)):
        return None
    try:
        if not math.isfinite(made_at) or made_at > now + CACHE_FUTURE_SECONDS:
            return None
        made_at = float(made_at)
    except OverflowError:  # an integer too large for a float
        return None
    text = document.get(key)
    if not isinstance(text, str):
        return None
    text = text[:max_chars].strip()
    return (made_at, text) if text else None


def _version(platform: dict[str, object]) -> str | None:
    value = platform.get("version")
    if isinstance(value, str) and RELEASE_VERSION.fullmatch(value):
        return value
    return None


def _branch(repo: dict[str, object], project_branch: str) -> str:
    """The repo's ``default_branch`` when it matches ``BRANCH_NAME``, else ``project_branch``."""
    value = repo.get("default_branch")
    if isinstance(value, str) and BRANCH_NAME.fullmatch(value):
        return value
    return project_branch


def _repos(value: object, project_branch: str) -> tuple[RepoEntry, ...]:
    items = value if isinstance(value, list) else []
    repos = [_object(item) for item in items]
    return tuple(
        RepoEntry(
            dir=_text(repo, "dir", ""),
            github=_text(repo, "github", ""),
            role=_text(repo, "role", RepoEntry.role),
            check_fast=_text(repo, "check_fast", ""),
            check_fast_timeout=_bounded_int(
                repo, "check_fast_timeout", CHECK_FAST_TIMEOUT_MIN, CHECK_FAST_TIMEOUT_MAX
            ),
            check_stop=_matching(repo, "check_stop", FREE_STRING),
            check=_text(repo, "check", ""),
            default_branch=_branch(repo, project_branch),
        )
        for repo in repos
        if _text(repo, "dir", "")
    )


def _settings_by_id(value: object) -> dict[str, dict[str, object]]:
    """``modules`` or ``doctor.rules``: each id whose settings are an object, minus comment keys."""
    return {key: _object(item) for key, item in _object(value).items() if isinstance(item, dict)}
